The grammar's fixtures for calc.ohm: the cases of ohm-go's
examples/generic-methods, and one input per operator.

The inputs:

s1: a number: 42
s2: an identifier: x
s3: times binds tighter than plus: 1 + 2 * 3
s4: parentheses override it: (1 + 2) * 3
s5: minus associates to the left: 10 - 4 - 3
s6: divide associates to the left: 8 / 2 / 2
s7: identifiers and numbers mixed: x * 2 + y
s8: nested parentheses: ((x))
s9: identifiers with digits: a1 / (b2 * 3)
s10: plus: 1 + 2
s11: minus: 5 - 2
s12: times: 3 * 4
s13: divide: 10 / 2
s14: the case of the PRD, section 5.3: (x + 3) * y - 10 / 2
e1: an operator with no right operand: 1 +
e2: a parenthesis that is not closed: (1 + 2

The expectations of s1 to s14 are candp's verbose parse trees without
terminals, builtins and lists (.t.l.b.v). e1 and e2 do not parse; each
expectation is the error message. docs/devtools/grammar-tests.md says
how to renew one.

-- @../../calc.ohm --
-- s1.txt --
42
-- s1.t.l.b.v.c_and_p --
(Exp 0-2 '42'
  (AddExp 0-2 '42'
    (MulExp 0-2 '42'
      (PriExp 0-2 '42'
        (number 0-2 '42'
        )
      )
    )
  )
)
-- s2.txt --
x
-- s2.t.l.b.v.c_and_p --
(Exp 0-1 'x'
  (AddExp 0-1 'x'
    (MulExp 0-1 'x'
      (PriExp 0-1 'x'
        (ident 0-1 'x'
        )
      )
    )
  )
)
-- s3.txt --
1 + 2 * 3
-- s3.t.l.b.v.c_and_p --
(Exp 0-9 '1 + 2 * 3'
  (AddExp 0-9 '1 + 2 * 3'
    (AddExp_plus 0-9 '1 + 2 * 3'
      (AddExp 0-1 '1'
        (MulExp 0-1 '1'
          (PriExp 0-1 '1'
            (number 0-1 '1'
            )
          )
        )
      )
      (MulExp 4-9 '2 * 3'
        (MulExp_times 4-9 '2 * 3'
          (MulExp 4-5 '2'
            (PriExp 4-5 '2'
              (number 4-5 '2'
              )
            )
          )
          (PriExp 8-9 '3'
            (number 8-9 '3'
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  )
)
